es).\n- #2 (Linux stable path only): fixed. The comment now states the limit.\n- #3 (night sweeps): fixed. The check is gated on `CLAUDE_NIGHT_SWEEP` the same way as the existing worktree line, and a test covers it.\n- #5 (the premise that a request means the buffer is saved): addressed. The rule now reads \"With autosave on, their request means their buffer is saved; without it, ask first\", and adds the take-the-pen announcement.\n- The hook wording \"The session offers once to set it for the author, waits for the answer, and edits that file only on a yes\" is declarative (rules/claude-code.md \u00a7 Hook output).\n\nFindings (no blocking finding; all consider):\n1. correctness + gaze, consider, scripts/on-start-context.sh:46: only whole-line `//` comments are stripped, so a commented-out setting still reads as on in three cases, each reproduced by gaze. The hook then stays silent while autosave is off:\n   - a trailing comment, as in `\"editor.fontSize\": 14, // \"files.autoSave\": \"afterDelay\"`\n   - a `/* \"files.autoSave\": \"afterDelay\" */` block\n   - a language-scoped `\"[markdown]\": {\"files.autoSave\": \"afterDelay\"}`\n   All three are rare in a user settings file. The cheap remedy is to word the code comment as \"whole-line `//`\" and accept the rest.\n2. gaze, consider, rules/prose/workpackages.md:16: \"without it, ask first\" depends on the agent knowing the autosave state. Its only signal is the hook line, and the hook is silent on macOS, Insiders, VSCodium and Remote-SSH, so there silence does not mean autosave is on. One remedy: \"unless autosave is known on, ask first\". Not required; the rule errs toward taking the pen.\n3. correctness, nofollow, tests/test_on_start_autosave.py:54: the `\"offers once to set it\"` assertion pins the wording of the hook line, which is acceptable.\n\nCheck: touched-tests selected 7 files (test_idh_lifecycle, test_on_start_autosave, test_on_start_live_counts, test_on_start_memory_injection, test_project_census, test_projection_validator, test_session_start_wiring); fallback: none; result: pass (163 passed).\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: 1m29s\ntelemetry: wall=~120s agents=1 tokens=n/a cost~=n/a\nseat: correctness \u00b7 runtime=claude-code \u00b7 family=anthropic \u00b7 route=unconfirmed \u00b7 model=anthropic/sonnet \u00b7 status: ran\n"}

